30,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I found out that people at the station block argued over broken latches! Also, some neighbors said they wouldn't turn away late bags. That's tricky!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Oh dear, the station block's bin house smells sour in the summer because you can't wash the floor. That sounds quite unpleasant for the neighbors.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The paperwork for a permanent build is extensive, requiring four months and five signatures. However, supervised mornings only take about fifty minutes per shift.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,I found out that the person living next to the bins complained eleven times! And some of our frontages are way too narrow for a bay!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The financial side is concerning. We spend 34,000 yen annually on maintenance, and a new shelter could cost over 140,000 yen even with a subsidy.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, eleven complaints is a lot! No wonder some people aren't talking. We really need to move the bins or change the rules.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Servas, that is a significant amount of money. I worry that a costly project might put a strain on some of our neighbors.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, the ""rules"" are only as good as the people enforcing them. If nobody wants to turn away late bags, supervision is useless.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, but if we move the bins, then everyone takes a turn being the ""bin house""! That's way more fair, right?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, fairness is not just about location, but also about what we can afford. We must be mindful of the different budgets in our lane.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, you're always so logical! But if we just rotate, maybe people will be nicer because they know they'll have the bins soon.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Rin, I agree that sharing the burden is kind. But I fear that moving the bins might just move the smell and the stress around.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, the current maintenance cost of 34,000 yen is a waste. We are paying for the consequences of an open-air system.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Shizue, but if we don't move them, the same person stays sad! We have to do something to make the ""bin neighbor"" happy!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance. We seek a solution that satisfies the heart, the wallet, and the clock.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
